      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_lookup_result_1a5e530bef09b9dc59f44888c60bdd82a0" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::vector&lt; <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_string_ref" kindref="compound">StringRef</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt;StringRef&gt; llvm::gsym::LookupResult::CallSiteFuncRegex</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>CallSiteFuncRegex</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::gsym::LookupResult::CallSiteFuncRegex</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_function" kindref="compound">Function</ref> name regex patterns associated with a call site at the lookup address. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This vector will be populated when:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>The lookup address matches a call site&apos;s return address in a function</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The call site has associated regex patterns that describe what functions can be called from that location</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>The regex patterns can be used to validate function calls during runtime checking or symbolication. For example:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Patterns like &quot;^foo$&quot; indicate the call site can only call function &quot;foo&quot;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Patterns like &quot;^std::&quot; indicate the call site can call any function in the std namespace</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Multiple patterns allow matching against a set of allowed functions</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The patterns are stored as string references into the GSYM string table. This information is typically loaded from:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>DWARF debug info call site entries</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>External YAML files specifying call site patterns</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Other debug info formats that encode call site constraints</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The patterns will be empty if:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>The lookup address is not at the return address of a call site</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The call site has no associated function name constraints</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Call site info was not included when creating the GSYM file </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/llvm/DebugInfo/GSYM/LookupResult.h" line="77" column="15" bodyfile="include/llvm/DebugInfo/GSYM/LookupResult.h" bodystart="77" bodyend="-1"/>
